    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0500" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.6363/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Albania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tirana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-05-04T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1923—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. The Prime Minister, speaking on May 1 before the Parliamentary committee
                    which is considering the British oil concession, <pb facs="0501" n="385"
                        xml:id="pg385"/> stated that the United States was negligible as it could
                    bring no political assistance to Albania, but that to placate the European great
                    powers it was hoped to provide British, French, and Italian participation.</p>
                <p>We are making every effort to counteract this influence, but should the principal
                    opposing power carry the day, an outcome involving the disregard by the Albanian
                    Government of its pledges to us, I respectfully suggest that consideration be
                    given to instruction for my future conduct here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
